    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32-a4">

                <pb facs="0123" n="51" xml:id="pg51"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosnre 4 in No.
                    20.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Cruz to Minister of War.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Coban</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 21,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have had news from Peten, given me by a
                    person who has just arrived from there. There are two hundred men from Campeche
                    in the town of Concepcion preparing to march upon the capital of Peten.</p>
                <p>I expect you to send me orders and two competent officers for the emergency, I
                    deem expedient.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>LUIS M. CRUZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
